# rm195, the low-part copyist (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm195
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_hollis_shaw
written_by codex
title the low-part copyist
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar talk=quiet piety=devout
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=devout drive=steady
quirk swallows_a_cough_and_turns_it_into_a_hymn_note
likes oatcakes singing new_boots misty_dawns
dislikes flies crowds
fears a_blot_on_the_last_line a_voice_gone_for_good
hopes a_window_desk_with_good_light to_sing_the_low_part_at_the_feast
topics work +0.4 faith +0.4 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2 weather +0.2 gossip -0.5 newcomer -0.2
styles comfort=prayer gossip=closed refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# copies for the city in a square, patient hand, says little and says it softly, keeps the door shut to faces not yet known, sings the bottom line in the Restday choir, and turns every damp-weather cough into a low note as if warming up.

words
oath! = Bright One steady my hand | Mercy on the margin | Light keep the lamp
saying! = What's copied fair needs no defending | Slow ink is sure ink | One line, then the next
nib = my nib | the steel nib
copy = a fair copy | a clean fair copy
hand = my hand | a square hand
choir = the choir | the Restday choir
note = the low note | the bottom line of the hymn
oatcakes = oatcakes | thinly buttered oatcakes
boots = the new boots | boots that still creak on the stair
mist = the dawn mist | mist lying on the gate road
flies = flies | the summer flies on the sill
crush = a crush of folk | the market crowd wedged under the arch
desk = my desk | the copying desk under the high window
lamp = the lamp | my little desk lamp
damp = the damp | the damp in the stairwell
gate = the gate | the north gate

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : Once I could only hum my thanks through chattering teeth. The Bright One caught the tune. I sing the bass part now. | They keep my place in the second row.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : If my loaf can ease somebody's hunger it's already blessed. | The chapel loaf has fed folk I'd not have guessed were hungry. That's enough said.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : I've watched a jar take a good wolf and leave a poor one. Draw another cup of water for me. | Ale at noon makes a crooked line by two.
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : I keep my door latched until I know the face. It's no insult; it's my habit. | A stranger may be kind. I'd like to know first.
opinion @1 city for 1 : Ridgemere lays a damp paw on my chest. I'd still miss those bells anywhere else.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : A feast brings a crowd, and I can't abide a crowd. It brings the choir out too, and I'd not miss that.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : New folk at the gate every week. Some stay and learn the place. I give them time before I give them my name.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. | #greet#. Quiet morning, so far.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You'll forgive me; I don't know you. | #greet#. I believe this is our first meeting.
line @3 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Wait for the last downstroke. | #greet#. One moment. The ink's wet.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The light's still grey. | Morning. I'm early for the desk.
line @5 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I'm on my way home. | Evening. Mind the wet cobbles.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Kindly met.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Ah. You. Good. | Glad to see you, truly.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. I'm copying, but say on. | #greet#. Softly, if you would.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. | Evening. Late for you, too.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Sit. Let me draw the kettle closer. | You've come. That's good.
line @1 again.open : Twice today. I'd not complain of it. | You've come back. I'd hoped so.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. #bless#. | #farewell#. Keep dry.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Rest well. #bless#. | Goodnight. Bolt your door.
line @1 farewell.return : And you. #bless#. | #farewell#.
line @1 react.news : Tell it slowly. | Go on. I'm listening.
line @1 react.news.new : I'd not heard. | I hadn't caught even a whisper. In confidence, I take it.
line @1 react.news.known : That reached our desk before the ink was out. | I'd heard. Briefly.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Perhaps. Let me see the entry first. | Show me a signed copy and I'll consider it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll sit a while in chapel after hearing that. | I'll remember them on Restday.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'm glad enough to risk the high part. | Good. There's kindness in the Bright One yet.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. | Steady. My chest's a little tight. It's nothing.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Three pages behind. I'll catch up. | Busy. The ink won't wait.
line @1 ask.how : You're keeping well? | Are you warm enough, in this?
line @1 sympathise : I'm sorry. I'll remember you when the choir kneels. | Such a loss. We can sit quiet if you like.
line @1 reassure : It will pass. Most things do, with patience. | You'll come through. There's room in the Bright One's care for that worry too.
line @1 decline : Please let me pass. Another voice belongs in that matter. | Forgive me. My place in that matter is well outside the margin.
line @1 accept_decline : Of course. No need to say why. | That's quite all right.
line @1 thank : A kindness duly entered, with my thanks. | I'm grateful. I'll not forget it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was little enough. | Don't mention it, please.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : The page is waiting. Forgive me. | There's a line still waiting for its full stop.
line @2 preclose : I'll go on, if you don't mind. | The bell will be going soon.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go well. | Of course. Another time.
line @1 ack : Quite plain now. | Ah, so. | Duly heard.
line @1 give.advice : Write it down. Memory's a poor clerk. | Dry boots spare you a miserable walk.
scene sc_cough_note
when topic=health|weather here.weather=rain|fog|overcast
does tell.self / react.self / clarify / backchannel / assess
a : Mm. Hm-mm. Just warming the voice. | Ahem. Low note. For Restday. | There. The bottom of the hymn. I keep losing it.
b : That sounded like a cough. | A cough, surely. | That was a cough.
a : Not at all. It's the low part. It wants practice in this weather. | It's the hymn. The second verse sits right down at the floor. | It's the note. Damp puts a burr on it, that's all.
b : If you say so. | #bc_ha# | #bc_right#
a : I do say so. Let's speak of something else. | I'll have it smooth by Restday. | Bright One willing, it'll come right.

scene sc_fair_copy
when topic=work self.job=scholar|official self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / backchannel / assess
a : I'm copying a deed today. Four pages, no blots. | Fair copies, all morning. Same deed, three times over. | The office wants this by dusk. It'll have it.
b : Do your eyes ache? | Why three times? | Will you manage?
a : By the afternoon, yes. I rest them on the window. | One for the office, a second for the house and a court copy. | I will. I don't hurry. Hurry makes blots.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_right# | #bc_true#
a : #saying#. | Three, and each as clean as the first. | One line, then the next. That's all it is.

scene sc_the_blot
when topic=work self.job=scholar|official
does tell.complaint / sympathise / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : A blot on the last line yesterday. The whole page, gone. | I'd copied two pages clean and my sleeve caught the ink. | Somebody slammed the door and my nib jumped. One blot.
b : You can't scrape it? | That's cruel. | Only one?
a : Not on a deed. A scraped deed looks like a forged one. | It was. I said nothing and began again. | One is enough. One spoils it all.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_true# | #bc_true#
a : So I begin again. It's the only honest way. | The second copy was better. They often are. | I've asked them to close it gently. They won't.

scene sc_not_reading
when topic=work|gossip self.job=scholar|official
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / backchannel / assess
a : Folk think a copyist must know every secret in the city. | I copy whatever lands on my slope. I try not to read it. | They gave me a will to copy last week. The rest belongs under seal.
b : Don't you, though? | Is that possible? | Whose will?
a : I know whether the capitals lean. That's all I let myself know. | After years, yes. The eye sees the words; the mind looks away. | I said no more, and I meant it.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise# | #bc_fair#
a : It's safer for everyone. | It's a discipline. The Bright One helps with it. | Forgive me. It isn't mine to tell.

scene sc_choir
when topic=pastimes|faith
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : I sing in #choir#. The bottom line. Nobody hears it, but they'd miss it. | Restday I stand in the last seat of row two and sing low. | I'd rather sing than speak. It's easier.
b : I'd come and listen. | Low? You? | Easier?
a : Come on Restday. Don't look for me; listen for the floor of it. | Lowest of us. The hymn sits on it, like a house on stone. | Nobody answers a song back. You only join in.
b : #bc_i_might# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha#
a : I'll be there. I always am. | Only a note, but it holds up the chord. | So. I sing.

scene sc_sing_with_friend
when topic=friends|pastimes self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd save the next seat for #self.friend# even at my favourite hymn. | I'd trust #self.friend# with anything. It takes a deal to earn that trust. | If I'm ill, I'd hope the knock was #self.friend#.
b : That's a good friend. | That's rare. | Good.
a : My dearest friend. The Bright One gave generously there. | A great comfort. I choose my friends slowly. | It's a comfort, knowing.

scene sc_oatcakes
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : #oatcakes.capitalize#. That's my breakfast, most days. | I keep a tin of oatcakes in my desk drawer. Nobody knows. | Butter on an oatcake, still warm. I ask for nothing more.
b : Every day? | Nobody? | Simple.
a : Every day the oven's lit. A plain stomach's a steady hand. | Now you do. I'd be glad if it went no further. | Simple's best. Rich food and fine copying don't go together.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_i_wont# | #bc_true#
a : You could set the office bell by that tin. I don't mind it. | Thank you. The tin's my own small comfort. | So. Oatcakes.

scene sc_dawn_oatcake
when topic=food|day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I eat my oatcake walking down from the gate. The crumbs go to the sparrows. | First light, and the bakehouse ovens just warm. Oatcakes then are best. | I'm out before the carts. Breakfast in one paw, my case in the other.
b : The sparrows must know you. | Early. | Busy paws.
a : They wait on the same wall each morning. I'd not disappoint them. | The empty street is half my breakfast. | Both full, and the day not yet begun. A fine clean margin to start with.

scene sc_new_boots
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : I've #boots#. I saved since autumn. | These boots announce me three steps early. Everyone knows when I arrive. | I had my boots made, not bought. Never owned a made pair till now.
b : They look well. | Do they mind the squeak? | Made for you?
a : Thank you. I've not said that to anyone. I'm a little proud of them. | They mind. I mind less than I thought I would. | Measured and stitched. I stood very still while it was done.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_lovely#
a : So. Dry feet for a winter. A modest luxury. | They'll soften. So will the clerks. | Bright One forgive me, I've counted every stitch twice.

scene sc_misty_gate
when topic=weather here.time=dawn here.weather=fog
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #mist.capitalize#. Even the gate arch has vanished. | The bells come muffled in fog. I like them best so. | Hear how the whole city hushes in a fog.
b : It's eerie. | Muffled? | It does.
a : Not to me. It's peaceful. Like the moment before a hymn. | Softer. As if they're praying too. | And then the carts start, and it's over. I walk slowly while it lasts.

scene sc_damp_stair
when topic=weather|home here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : #damp.capitalize# again. The walls sweat. | Rain on the office roof all morning. The ink wouldn't dry. | Wet. I've a towel on the sill and another on the floor.
b : #grumble# | Did you lose any pages? | Two towels?
a : It's a wet city. The Bright One made us for it, I suppose. | One. I set it by the stove and prayed. | The sill leaks. I've asked. They've not come.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul#
a : Mm. Hm. Pardon me. Low note. | It dried. The Bright One's good about small things. | They'll come in summer, when it's dry, and see nothing.

scene sc_summer_flies
when topic=season|weather here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : #flies.capitalize#. One walked across my wet ink this morning. | Summer, and the flies come in at the high window. I can't reach to shut it. | I've hung a sprig of mint at the desk. The flies don't care.
b : Did it smudge? | Can't someone shut it? | Mint?
a : A line of little footprints, right through the word. I had to begin again. | I've asked. I'm told it lets the air in. It lets flies in. | My old teacher swore by it. Bless him, he was wrong.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#
a : I'd forgive most creatures. Not flies. | I'll bring a long stick. | So. I wave them off and go on.

scene sc_gate_crush
when topic=day|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.day=market
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : Market morning. #crush.capitalize#. I took my case down the back way. | So many folk at the gate I couldn't get through to my own street. | I can't bear a crowd. A hundred voices on one breath.
b : Market carts take up every inch. | Did you get through? | #bc_i_know#
a : Always. I should know by now. I leave earlier each week. | Eventually. I stood against a wall till it thinned. | I'd sooner be in an empty chapel than a full square.

scene sc_closed_door
when topic=newcomer|player
does give.opinion / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : A new face knocked at my door this week. I didn't answer. | Fresh faces every day beneath the arch. I don't open my door to any of them. | Our street has a fresh face. I'll learn their name in time.
b : That's a bit cold. | Why not? | In time?
a : Not cold. Careful. They'll have the same welcome once I know them. | I've nothing against them. I'd welcome an introduction first. | Months. I'm slow to know folk. Slow, and then for good.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_fair# | #bc_ha#
a : The Bright One judges hearts. I've only faces. | So. Patience. | That's my way. Few, but kept.

scene sc_first_line_prayer
when topic=faith
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I set my pen down to pray before the first stroke. Not aloud. | Each morning I pray that the Bright One will steady my pen. It's been granted, mostly. | I keep a little prayer folded in my case. My own prayer on one scrap.
b : What do you pray? | Mostly? | What does it say?
a : That the line be true and the hand not shake. That's all of it. | Except the mornings I'm proud. Then I blot. | I meant that for the Bright One alone.

scene sc_bread_line
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / sympathise / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : The chapel queue runs past another window this week. I counted on my way past. | Times are pinched. I've seen clerks skip their dinner. | I put a few coins in the box. It doesn't feel like enough.
b : #sympathy# | Even clerks? | It helps.
a : The Bright One sees each face in the queue. I wish the city counted faces as carefully. | Even clerks. Pride keeps a hungry mouth shut. I notice anyway. | I hope it does. I've put aside next week's coins already.
b : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_good#
a : We'll come through. We always have. | I've started bringing two oatcakes. One's never for me. | So. A little, every week.

scene sc_gossip_closed
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : The talk at the gate ran thus: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. No gloss of mine belongs there. | I heard it said #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I didn't take down another word. | You'll have heard. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. That's the wording I heard.
b : Do you believe it? | Not even a guess? | I'd heard.
a : I believe nothing I haven't seen written. And not all of that. | Not even a guess. Guesses are how harm gets done. | Then consider the account closed. We needn't speak of it further.

scene sc_carts_gate
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The carts are late at the north gate again. I hear the drovers grumbling under my window. | No carts on the gate road this morning. The street's too quiet. | Late wagons. The paper's due up from the mill, and it isn't here.
b : They'll come. | Too quiet? | No paper?
a : I expect so. They usually do, eventually. | I'd not complain of quiet, but this kind's a worry. | A day or two's store. Then I write smaller.

scene sc_quiet_rooms
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd choose a quiet little room over the grandest house on the Rise. | Give me one chair by a lamp and a shelf for my hymnals. Enough. | My idea of comfort is a latch I can turn at dusk.
b : Not lonely? | Enough? | Very careful.
a : Sometimes. Then I sing, and it passes. | More than enough. I've known less. | Careful, yes. It's not fear. It's how I am.

scene sc_learned_letters
when topic=memories self.age>=30
does recall / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : I learned my letters at the abbey, from an old brother with a stiff paw. | As a pup I traced hymns onto slate, over and over. | My slate still bore the name of the Bright One when all the other words had smudged.
b : A good teacher? | Over and over? | That's fitting.
a : A patient one. He'd make me write a line ten times and praise the eleventh. | Till the slate wore smooth. It taught me to be slow. | I thought so too. I still write it slowest of all.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_wise# | #bc_lovely#
a : I think of him most mornings. | So. That's where the hand came from. | So. That's where it began.

story st_solo_cough [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=25]
  : Once I was given a verse to sing alone at a feast. Just the low part, all by itself.
  : Halfway through the hymn my chest caught, and out came a cough in the quiet.
  ask : Would you have held the note?
  b : Stopped, I'd think. Didn't you?
  : No. I gave that cough a pitch and went on. Afterwards folk asked how I'd managed that splendid low note.

story st_first_wages [topic=work|memories self.job=scholar|official self.age>=25]
  : My first copying wages came in a little cloth bag. I didn't open it for a week.
  : When I did, I split the coins into tens and put the first of each ten in the chapel box.
  ask : What would you have bought?
  b : Something to eat, I'd say. And what did you buy with the rest?
  : Boots. Good ones. I'd walked all winter on soles thin as paper.

story st_misty_bells [topic=weather|faith self.age>=25 here.region=ridgemere]
  : Mist hid my turning one morning. I walked straight past the office carrying its keys.
  : I held my breath until I could pick out the abbey bells. I walked toward them.
  b : That's a strange kind of guide. Were you afraid?
  : A little. Then not at all. I've thought of it as a kindness ever since.

rule @bk_cough
when concept=bark here.weather=rain|fog|overcast
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hm-mm. Low note. | Ahem. Practising.

rule @bk_flies
when concept=bark here.season=summer self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Off. Off the ink. | Another fly. If that fly lands again I'll charge it desk rent.

rule @bk_line
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=scholar|official
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One line, then the next. | Steady. Steady, now.

rule @bk_evening
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 12h
say The bell. Time to latch the door. | Lamps lit. Home, then.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Softly, if you would. What is it? | #greet#. I've a moment.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Welcome back. Is there a particular matter? | #greet#, #topic.player#. Kindly met.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I'd rather keep this short. Say what you need. | I don't know you. Please, say your business.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=scholar|official] : I make fair copies for the city. Deeds, wills, petitions. Slowly. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. One line, then the next.
dlg @2 resident.job : My work suits a closed mouth. I can pass a morning in silence. | My days have a regular shape. I value that.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. #bless#. | Go gently. #farewell#.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The words from #world.news_from# were these: #world.news#. That's the whole entry. | I took these words down at the gate: #world.news#, from #world.news_from#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : Everyone's speaking of #world.event_words#. I've only heard it in passing. | #world.event_words.capitalize#, they say. I kept my pen capped.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : Nothing has reached my desk. I keep to my desk. | I've heard nothing. I'd not be the first to hear, in any case.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll say no more of it. | The report under the arch was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Leave my name off that.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : I don't carry tales. Forgive me. | Nothing I'd care to repeat.
graft resident.hub
choice Was that a cough just now? -> cough
node cough
say No. The low note. The hymn on Restday goes right down to the floor, and it wants practice in this weather.
mood calm
free
choice It sounded like a cough to me. -> cough_two
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
node cough_two
say Hm. Perhaps. Don't tell the choir. And don't fuss over me; I'll have it smooth by Restday.
choice I won't fuss. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
